WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.438
For this guided practice predict before you run
Compare the unparenthesized rule

00:00:05.462 --> 00:00:10.100
with the parenthesized rule Because AND binds before
OR Version A allows

00:00:10.125 --> 00:00:13.525
any patient age sixty-five or older even when
consent is not true

00:00:14.412 --> 00:00:19.138
Version B applies the consent requirement to both
alternatives Look for the

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:23.962
record that satisfies the age condition but has
false consent That record

00:00:23.988 --> 00:00:27.875
should appear only in Version A The purpose is not
just to

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:33.538
identify the row Explain which subexpression
admitted it If you can

00:00:33.562 --> 00:00:37.250
say that the age branch was evaluated independently
of consent because AND

00:00:37.275 --> 00:00:40.712
bound to the diagnosis branch you understand the
precedence problem
